title: Arrival at the gates
story: fernhill
description: The opening beat — the notice, the letter, the weathervane in its
  evening voice, and the walk up the drive to the Fountain Court.
seed: 1

---

# The `first time` block REPLACES the standing description on the first visit
# rather than preceding it — the wrought-iron sentence is not here yet.
> look
[OK: contains "The cab is already grinding away down the lane"]
[OK: contains "BY ORDER OF THE ESTATE, AT DAWN"]
[OK: not contains "Wrought-iron gates stand open"]

# Second look, same visit: now the standing description, and the opening is gone
# for good.
> look
[OK: contains "Wrought-iron gates stand open on one hinge apiece"]
[OK: not contains "The cab is already grinding away"]

# Both documents state the stakes: the deed has to be produced before dawn.
> read the auction notice
[OK: contains "Sale to be conducted at the property at first light"]

> read the letter
[OK: contains "must produce the original deed of the estate"]

# The weathervane is the phrasebook probe (ADR-250). At evening, the mood line
# comes from the evening-voice book, and this is its first-time variant.
> examine the weathervane
[OK: contains "An iron weathervane on the gatepost"]
[OK: contains "The vane noses the evening breeze, unhurried"]

# vane-story is story text; no book may beat it, in either state.
> push the weathervane
[OK: contains "creaks the same one story it always tells"]

# vane-quiet is covered only by the evening book — see phrasebooks.transcript
# for what midnight does to each of these three lines.
> touch the weathervane
[OK: contains "The vane keeps its own counsel"]

# South is blocked by story text, not by a missing exit.
> south
[OK: contains "The lane runs three dark miles to the village"]
[OK: not contains "Gravel Drive"]
[STATE: true, player.location = Iron Gates]

> north
[OK: contains "Gravel Drive"]
[OK: contains "The drive curves between bare lime trees"]
[EVENT: true, type="if.event.actor_moved"]

> examine the lime trees
[OK: contains "Bare pollarded limes"]

> north
[OK: contains "Fountain Court"]
[OK: contains "A paved court before the front door"]

# Tobias is on patrol and reaches the court on his round.
> examine the fountain
[OK: contains "A dry stone basin drifted with last summer"]
[STATE: true, player.location = Fountain Court]
